<h1>Terms and conditions</h1>
<section class="panel">
    <h2>About this service</h2>
    <p>Xenon is a moderation administration interface. This deployment is operated by its service operator, not necessarily by the Xenon software author or contributors. The operator is responsible for this service, its moderation policies and decisions, and any additional deployment-specific terms.</p>
    <p>These general terms describe permitted use of the interface. They do not identify the operator or replace information the operator must provide under applicable law. Review the operator's published contact details, moderation policy and any supplementary terms before using the service.</p>
    <h2>Access and account security</h2>
    <p>Administrative access requires an authenticated Bluesky identity and an active team membership with the necessary permissions. Signing in does not itself grant administrative authority. Access may be limited, suspended or removed by the operator.</p>
    <p>Use only your own authorized identity, protect your sign-in session, and sign out on shared devices. Do not share session cookies, tokens, private keys or other credentials.</p>
    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Use the service lawfully and only within your assigned role. Do not attempt to bypass authorization, access information you are not permitted to see, interfere with service availability, or submit malicious or knowingly misleading material.</p>
    <p>Submit only information necessary for moderation. Do not place passwords, tokens, private keys or unrelated sensitive personal information in reports, notes or audit reasons. Treat nonpublic reports and case information as confidential and disclose them only when authorized and lawful.</p>
    <h2>Moderation actions and review</h2>
    <p>Review the exact account or record, label value, record version where applicable, and stated reason before confirming an action. Labels, decisions and membership changes can have lasting effects and are recorded by the service.</p>
    <p>Reports do not automatically establish wrongdoing or issue labels. Decisions and appeals are handled under the operator's moderation policy; an appeal does not guarantee a particular outcome. Contact the operator through its published channels to request review.</p>
    <p>Where public label distribution is enabled, other services may retain and act on published labels. Negating a label, closing a case or deleting local data does not guarantee removal of copies held elsewhere.</p>
    <h2>Availability and software</h2>
    <p>Availability, response times and compatibility with external identity and protocol services are not guaranteed. Maintenance, failures or changes to those services can interrupt access. Stop and contact the operator if an outcome is unclear rather than assuming a failed request made no change.</p>
    <p>The source code is available under the <a href="https://github.com/blowdart/idunno.Bluesky/blob/main/LICENSE">repository's MIT license</a>. That software license is separate from the operator's terms for using this hosted service. Nothing on this page excludes rights or obligations that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>
    <h2>Privacy and changes</h2>
    <p>Read the <a asp-area="Xenon" asp-page="/Privacy">privacy notice</a> for information about authentication, moderation records and disclosures. The operator is responsible for communicating material changes to its terms and policies, including any effective dates required by law.</p>
</section>
